      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=\\frac{7}{{t}^{3}}+{t}^{2}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{7}{{t}^{3}}+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{{t}^{4}}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{21}{{t}^{4}}+2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{84}{{t}^{5}}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
